.TH LINUX-THERMAL-SECURE-BOOT-SETUP 8 "2026-08-21" "linux-thermal-control 0.5.13" "System Administration"
.SH NAME
linux-thermal-secure-boot-setup \- enroll and verify the acpi_call module-signing key
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B linux-thermal-secure-boot-setup
.RI [ --prepare | --status | --help ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Prepares the DKMS-built
.B acpi_call
module for use while UEFI Secure Boot and Shim validation remain enabled.
The prepare operation creates Ubuntu's shared DKMS machine-owner key when necessary,
rebuilds the module for the running kernel, and requests enrollment of the
public certificate through MokManager.
.PP
Enrollment deliberately requires physical confirmation at the next boot. The
private key is never added to firmware and remains root-owned under
.IR /var/lib/shim-signed/mok .
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B --prepare
Prepare and sign the module, then request MOK enrollment. This operation must
be run as root and is the default.
.TP
.B --status
Report UEFI Secure Boot state, MOK enrollment, and the installed module signer.
.TP
.B --help
Show command usage.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /var/lib/shim-signed/mok/MOK.priv
Machine-specific private module-signing key.
.TP
.I /var/lib/shim-signed/mok/MOK.der
Public certificate enrolled through MokManager.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR mokutil (1),
.BR dkms (8),
.BR modprobe (8),
.BR update-secureboot-policy (8)
